<!--
  The MONITORING key's mark: `monitoring`, from M ICON.

  E46M3 /// MONITORING is the MONITORING category's tool, and in TSUNAGI///M the
  category word IS the mark (tsunagi-m-release §3.2): three stepped slits with a
  read-out line entering from each side.

  Geometry: the eight quadrilaterals read out of
  `M ICON/icons/monitoring-1024.png`, scaled to the 24-unit viewport the console
  icons use. This is the WIDER of the two marks on this console at 94% of the
  viewport, so it sets the shared scale and `mapping` (d_ic_tuner) is drawn
  smaller to match rather than the other way round — per-mark scaling would break
  the family (tsunagi-m-release §4.1).

  One flat tone, like every icon here: @color/d_icon by day, @color/d_icon_night
  at night, swapped by ConsoleKeys.applyNight with a SRC_IN filter. The declared
  colour only matters before the first swap; naming the same token keeps the two
  in step.

  ## This key carries no lamp

  The two outermost paths are the mark's read-out lines, not a status
  indication. A lamp on this console reports whether a LINK is up (docs/04 §5),
  and MONITORING is a web tool reached through Chrome — it is not a link to a
  device, any more than TUNER is. Both keys are lampless for the same reason.
-->
